# batch 1: WA (WSDOT M 41-10, 2027 edition per page headers) and TX (TxDOT 2024). Read 2026-11-20 via WebFetch.
U='https://wsdot.wa.gov/publications/manuals/fulltext/M41-10/Division7.pdf'
S='WSDOT Standard Specifications for Road, Bridge, and Municipal Construction, M 41-10, 2027 edition, Division 7 (read 2026-11-20)'
ED='2027'
add('spec-wa-trench-1','WA','Washington WSDOT pipe trench, bedding and backfill numbers (Section 7-08)',
"Washington (WSDOT Standard Specifications M 41-10, 2027 edition, Section 7-08, general pipe installation). Trench: remove ledge rock, boulders and stones to give at least 6 inches clearance under all parts of the pipe; keep the toe of the spoil pile at least 2 feet from the trench edge; shoring is called for in trenches 4 feet or deeper that don't meet the open-pit rules of 3-07.3(3)B (7-08.3(1)A). Bedding: compact to 90 percent of maximum density, in lifts no more than 6 inches thick along the sides of the pipe; fix line and grade by scraping or filling under the barrel, never by blocking or wedging (7-08.3(1)C). Backfill (7-08.3(3)): pipe zone compacted to 90 percent, no rocks or lumps over 3 inches; under existing pavement or roadways 6-inch layers at 95 percent; in non-traffic areas 6-inch layers at 85 percent. No tractors or heavy equipment over the pipe until backfill is 3 feet above the top of the pipe. Laying tolerance: invert within plus or minus 0.03 foot at the time of backfill, and never a reverse slope (7-08.3(2)B). Your contract's special provisions and the city's own amendments can change these numbers.",S,U,ED)
add('spec-wa-stormtest-1','WA','Washington WSDOT storm sewer tests (Section 7-04)',
"Washington (WSDOT M 41-10, 2027 edition, Section 7-04.3(1), storm sewers). Exfiltration test: leakage no more than 1 gallon per hour per inch of diameter per 100 feet, with at least 6 feet of water above the crown; the allowance rises 10 percent for each extra 2 feet of head, and pressure at the low-end invert is capped at 16 feet of water (7-04.3(1)B). Infiltration test: no more than 0.8 gallon per hour per inch of diameter per 100 feet (7-04.3(1)C). Low-pressure air test: the pressure-drop time must be at least the table time, for example 80 seconds for 100 feet of 12-inch pipe; pipe that does not pass air (plastic, lined) needs four times the table time; pipe over 30 inches is tested joint by joint under ASTM C1103 (7-04.3(1)E and F). Sanitary sewers are stricter: see Section 7-17.",S,U,ED)
add('spec-wa-sewertest-1','WA','Washington WSDOT sanitary sewer tests: air, water, mandrel, TV (Section 7-17)',
"Washington (WSDOT M 41-10, 2027 edition, Section 7-17.3(2), sanitary sewers). Finish cleaning and testing within 15 working days after backfilling. Exfiltration: no more than 0.28 gallon per hour per inch of diameter per 100 feet, with 6 feet of head over the crown at the upper end (or over groundwater if higher), test length no more than 700 feet, no more than 16 feet of head at the low invert (7-17.3(2)B). Infiltration: 0.16 gallon per hour per inch per 100 feet when groundwater head is 2 feet or less (7-17.3(2)C). Add 0.2 gallon per hour per foot of head for each manhole in the test section (D). Low-pressure air test for pipe 30 inches and smaller: pump to 4 psig, wait at least 2 minutes, then time the drop from 3.5 to 2.5 psig; the time comes from K = 0.0111 x d squared x L and C = 0.0003918 x d x L (E); pipe that does not pass air needs four times that time (F); over 30 inches test each joint under ASTM C1103. Deflection test for thermoplastic pipe: not less than 30 days after trench backfill and compaction are complete, with a mandrel that has an odd number of legs (9 or more) and is 95 percent of the pipe's base inside diameter (G). TV inspection can be required by the Engineer before final acceptance (H).",S,U,ED)
add('spec-wa-water-1','WA','Washington WSDOT water main: cover, backfill, pressure test, disinfection (Section 7-09)',
"Washington (WSDOT M 41-10, 2027 edition, Section 7-09, water mains). Minimum cover 36 inches over the top of the pipe; at least 1 foot over valve operating nuts. Trench width up to 1 foot above the pipe: no more than 30 inches or 1.5 times the pipe outside diameter plus 18 inches, whichever is greater. Bedding compacted to 95 percent of maximum density (7-09.3(9)); backfill to at least 95 percent, in layers of 6 inches loose or less under paved areas (7-09.3(11)). Hydrostatic test (7-09.3(23)): 150 psi above operating pressure and never less than 225 psi; sections normally no longer than 1,500 feet; pump up, stop for 15 minutes, pump back to test pressure; allowable leakage L = S x D x square root of P / 266,400 (L gallons per hour, S feet of pipe, D inches, P psi). Disinfection (7-09.3(24)): at least 50 mg/L chlorine to start, hold at least 24 hours, at least 25 mg/L left after 24 hours; flush at 2.5 feet per second or more; dechlorinate the flush water to 0.1 ppm or less and pH 6.5 to 8.5. Services 2 inch and smaller need 3 feet of cover (7-15); hydrants need a 3-foot clear radius and the sidewalk flange 2 inches above finished grade (7-14).",S,U,ED)
add('spec-wa-structures-1','WA','Washington WSDOT manholes, catch basins, side sewers and cleanouts (Sections 7-05, 7-18, 7-19)',
"Washington (WSDOT M 41-10, 2027 edition). Manholes, inlets and catch basins (7-05): dig to leave 1 foot clear between the structure and the bank; ladder rungs at 12 inches; rigid pipe entering a sanitary manhole needs a flexible joint within 1.5 pipe diameters or 18 inches of the wall, whichever is greater; manholes over 10 feet are paid per extra foot; an abandoned manhole is broken down to at least 4 feet below the new surface and filled with sand compacted to 90 percent. Side sewers (7-18): joint deflection never more than 2 inches per foot, use 1/8 bends for bigger turns; a 6-inch test tee goes where the side sewer crosses the right-of-way line; mark the end with a 2x4 stake 4 feet long buried 3 feet. Cleanouts (7-19): at each total 90 degrees of change in grade or alignment, never more than 100 feet apart, same size as the side sewer.",S,U,ED)

U='https://www.txdot.gov/content/dam/docs/specifications/2024/2024-specifications-400-series.pdf'
S='TxDOT Standard Specifications for Construction and Maintenance of Highways, Streets, and Bridges, 2024, Items 400, 401, 402 (read 2026-11-20)'
ED='2024'
add('spec-tx-trench-1','TX','Texas TxDOT pipe excavation, bedding and backfill (Items 400, 401, 402)',
"Texas (TxDOT 2024 Standard Specifications). Item 400, Excavation and Backfill for Structures: pipe gets Class C bedding unless the plans show something else; for precast concrete pipe the ASTM C1479 beddings are allowed (400.3.2). Pipe backfill goes in uniform layers no more than 8 inches deep (loose), each lift compacted mechanically, with the haunches thoroughly compacted (400.3.3.3); each layer must meet the density required for the roadbed (400.3.3.1; the percent comes from the embankment item and the plans, not Item 400). Cement-stabilized backfill: at least 7 percent cement by dry weight of aggregate, placed and compacted within 2 hours of mixing (400.3.3.4). Flowable backfill (Item 401, Table 2): excavatable mix 80 to 200 psi at 28 days; non-excavatable over 200 psi. Trench protection (Item 402): furnish and place excavation protection for trenches 5 feet or greater in depth, following OSHA 29 CFR 1926 Subpart P.",S,U,ED)
S='TxDOT Standard Specifications, 2024, Items 460, 462, 464 (read 2026-11-20)'
add('spec-tx-pipe-1','TX','Texas TxDOT concrete pipe, metal pipe and box culverts (Items 460, 462, 464)',
"Texas (TxDOT 2024 Standard Specifications). Item 464, Reinforced Concrete Pipe: circular pipe Classes I through V (D-loads 800 to 3,000); joints may be mortar, cold-applied asphalt joint compound, rubber gaskets (ASTM C1619 Class A or C) or preformed flexible sealant (ASTM C990); arch and elliptical pipe need at least 1 foot of cover; do not run heavy earth-moving equipment over the pipe until at least 4 feet of compacted fill is in place unless the plans or the Engineer allow it in writing (464.3.1). Item 460, Corrugated Metal Pipe: lay from the outlet end with laps pointing upstream; same 4-foot rule for heavy earth-moving equipment (460.3.2); bell-and-spigot gaskets to ASTM F477 with at least a 6-inch stab depth. Item 462, Concrete Box Culverts: no more than four lifting holes per precast section, each 3 inches or smaller; boxes with joints that are not mortar can be backfilled right away. Jacking, boring or tunneling any of these is under Item 476.",S,U,ED)
